Third-party material (NOT covered by the MIT licence above)

The MIT licence applies to the team's own code, worlds, media and documentation.
It does not apply to Hiwonder's material, which keeps its own licence / terms of use:

  * The Hiwonder JetArm ROS 2 packages (jetarm_6dof_description, robot_gazebo,
    robot_moveit_config: robot URDF/xacro, meshes, controller configuration, launch
    files). They are NOT included in this repository; get them from Hiwonder (see
    README.md, "Installation"). Their package.xml files declare no licence
    ("TODO: License declaration"; robot_moveit_config says BSD).
  * Files in this repository that are derived from Hiwonder's files keep Hiwonder's
    terms for the Hiwonder-derived parts:
      - robot_gazebo/urdf/jetarm_mecanum.gazebo.xacro (instantiates Hiwonder's arm,
        gripper and camera macros; the ros2_control / joint-state plugin blocks follow
        Hiwonder's robot.gazebo.xacro)
      - robot_gazebo/urdf/jetarm_mecanum_system.gazebo.xacro (generated; includes the file above)
      - robot_gazebo/launch/hospital.launch.py, robot_gazebo/launch/hospital_system.launch.py
        (structure follows Hiwonder's worlds.launch.py / spawn_model.launch.py and they
        include Hiwonder's ros_ign_bridge.launch.py)
    The arm kinematics in scripts/jetarm_pick_place.py use the link dimensions of
    Hiwonder's URDF.
